#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kfouleggs; is a clone of the Japanese PuyoPuyo game, with advanced features "
"such as multiplayer games against human or <acronym>AI</acronym>. If you "
"have played <application>Tetris</application>, or one of its many clones, "
"you will find &kfouleggs; easy to learn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a New Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kfouleggs;, just click on the <guibutton>Start </guibutton> "
"button, or select <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>Game</"
"guimenu> menu at any time to start a new game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Aim of the Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The aim of the game is to achieve the highest score possible by moving the "
"falling tiles in such a way that tiles of the same color are adjacent, and "
"disappear. The more tiles you remove, the higher your score."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playing the Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <keycap>Left</keycap> and <keycap>Right</keycap> arrow keys to move "
"the falling tile in the relevant direction, and the <keycap>Up</keycap> "
"arrow and <keycap>Return</keycap> keys to rotate the tile left and right "
"respectively. The <keycap>Shift</keycap> key drops the tile down one line, "
"and the <keycap>Down</keycap> key drops the tile all the way down - use it "
"as a way of saving time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All of these shortcuts can be customized by selecting <guimenuitem>Configure "
"Shortcuts...</guimenuitem> from the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If two or more tiles of the same color come to rest horizontally or "
"vertically next to each other, they become <quote>glued</quote>. If four or "
"more pieces of the same color come to be <quote>glued</quote>, they "
"disappear, and any pieces above them fall down according to the law of "
"gravity ;-). If this causes four or more pieces to become <quote>glued</"
"quote>, then they will also disappear, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every time you remove 100 tiles, you advance to the next level, where the "
"tiles fall faster, and the game is more difficult."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "The game ends when the central column fills with tiles, and no more can fall."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Game Screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kfouleggs; in Action"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "A quick explanation of what each of the parts of the game screen are for..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Along the left hand side, from top to bottom:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Score"
msgstr "Marca"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows your current score."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Puyos"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows the number of removed sets of pieces."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Level"
msgstr "Nivèl"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shows the number of the level you are currently on. The first, easiest level "
"is level one, progressing to the last, hardest level, 20."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the center is the area where the action takes place. The tiles fall "
"through the rectangle (whose properties can be changed in "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure KFoulEggs...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, see <xref linkend=\"game-config\"/>) until "
"reaching the bottom. The two small black rectangles under the main one are "
"the tile's <quote>shadow</quote> which show where it will land. You can "
"toggle the tile's shadow in <xref linkend=\"game-config\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right hand side, the <guilabel>Next Tile</guilabel> box shows what "
"the next tile to fall will be, if you have enabled it in <xref linkend="
"\"game-config\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kfouleggs; Configuration and Default Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Gameplay"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kfouleggs; configuration is accessed from "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kfouleggs;..."
"</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. The options are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "Initial level:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the level which you will play at startup, from 1 (easiest) to 20 "
"(hardest). Default is level one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Direct drop down"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, pressing the <keysym>Down Arrow</keysym> will cause a tile to "
"immediately fall to the bottom of the screen. If unchecked, pressing the "
"<keysym>Down Arrow</keysym> only causes the piece to fall until the key is "
"released."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable animations"
msgstr "Activar las animacions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, pieces are shown with an animation (a small rebound effect), "
"when they touch the bottom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show piece's shadow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, a shadow is placed beneath the game board showing where the "
"piece will fall."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show next piece"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, shows the next tile that will fall onto the game board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show detailed \"removed lines\" field"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If checked, the <guilabel>Puyos</guilabel> counter on the left of the screen "
"shows how many times each number of Puyos have been removed. If unchecked, "
"just the total number removed is shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background"
msgstr "Fons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the color and the opacity for &kfouleggs; background. An opacity of "
"zero makes the &kfouleggs; background completely transparent, and a setting "
"of one makes the &kfouleggs; background completely opaque."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Colors Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can select the colors used for the tiles in &kfouleggs;."
msgstr ""

